The suspected component (mswitch1 uplink trunk carrying VLAN 10/20) is healthy. Evidence: on mswitch1 the VLAN bridges br_vlan10 and br_vlan20 are up with member subinterfaces on both uplink-facing ports (eth0.10/.20 toward switch1 and eth4.10/.20 toward router0). Interface counters on eth4.10/eth4.20 and eth0.10/eth0.20 show bidirectional traffic, and ethtool reports link detected: yes on both eth0 and eth4. On switch1, the matching trunk subinterfaces eth0.10 and eth0.20 are up and enslaved to br_vlan10/br_vlan20. On router0, the router-on-a-stick SVIs eth0.10 (172.16.10.1) and eth0.20 (172.16.20.1) are up; ARP shows PC4 and Laptop0 MACs, and we can ping from PC4 to its gateway (172.16.10.1) and from router0 to PC4.
